      "There was a leather notebook in the inn drawer where João noted, without names, who had seen the trail and what they said upon returning. It was not a curiosity archive — it was a record of trust. 'Woman, autumn, brother,' he had written of Marina. 'Asked for nothing more.' Those lines were enough to remember that the valley changed lives without needing public testimony.",
      "Tourists sometimes tried to bribe João for a 'secret route.' He refused politely and offered tea. 'The mountain does not accept advance payment,' he said. 'It charges presence.' Most laughed, thinking it poetic. Those who grew serious were, almost always, those the trail would one day call — even if not that season.",
      "In the valley, the spring water never froze, even when the entire range hardened with frost. João measured the temperature once out of scientific curiosity: four degrees above expected, constant. He kept the data in the notebook and added: 'Some things do not need explanation to be true.'",
      "A documentary crew wanted to film the golden sunset. João allowed the official overlook but hid the path to the gap by walking more slowly than necessary until the light closed. The footage was beautiful and empty — exactly what protected the place. The director complained; the cinematographer, years later, returned alone and thanked him in silence at the village bar.",
      "Mateus discovered that the 'guide's chair' warmed before any other stone in the valley, as if it held memory of seated bodies. He began leaving a folded blanket there for whoever arrived trembling from cold or emotion. It was the kind of detail João would make without announcing — practical inheritance of an invisible craft.",
      "The last time Marina climbed, she did not enter the valley. She stopped at the gap, touched the rock, waved to Mateus, and descended. 'I have already learned,' she said on the way back. João, alive, would have smiled. Some places do not need to be revisited to remain true; they only need to have existed at the right hour.",
